%% Updated 2026-06-26.
%% Purpose: Proposal status lifecycle
%% Scope: TaskApplication-backed proposal state transitions
%% Excludes: Assignment rules (see act_01c), ranking (see act_02d)
%% Related: task_assignment_rules.ts:canApplyForTask, canProcessApplication

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> pending : User sends proposal\n(message, portfolio_links)\ncanApplyForTask checks:\n• not own task\n• public visibility\n• not assigned\n• not past deadline\n• no duplicate

    pending --> approved : Creator or project\nowner/manager approves\n→ Create TaskAssignment\n→ Auto-reject others
    pending --> rejected : Creator or project\nowner/manager rejects\n(with rejection_reason)
    pending --> withdrawn : Contributor withdraws\n(own pending only)

    approved --> [*]
    rejected --> [*]
    withdrawn --> [*]

    note right of pending
        POLICY: canProcessApplication allows
        task creator OR project owner/manager.

        RUNTIME GAP: ProcessMarketplaceApplicationCommand
        currently only passes creator context.
        See risk-log R-01.
        ──────────────────
        Approving does NOT change task status.
        Task stays in current status.
        Assignee must manually start work.
    end note

    note left of approved
        On approval (ProcessMarketplaceApplicationCommand):
        • INSERT task_assignment (status=active)
        • SET task.assigned_to = contributor/applicant_id
        • Reject all other pending proposals
        • Audit event
        • Notify contributor
    end note
